Clone each realm-local registered handle under a short registry borrow before
borrowing the handle value. This makes the unsafe extended Ref lifetime derive
from the same Rc retained by the returned guard, while registry removal stays
independent from access to the registered value.

The JS engine can terminate a guest by trapping across a Rust host callback,
and that boundary is not guaranteed to run every Rust destructor. Use fallible
inner borrows so a stranded handle guard becomes absence, and make both
callback_signal handle acquisitions translate that conflict to the existing
terminal WASI Fault outcome. Registry borrow invariant violations still panic;
this does not suppress unrelated reentrant registry mutation.

